+// script execution (not just mid-init) elsewhere. That would need classic
+// mode to skip its per-request tsrm_shutdown() whenever another TSRM
+// context is alive — a larger change we haven't made here. In practice the
+// worker only ever boots after persistent mode has already succeeded (see
+// MainActivity.initializeEnvironmentAsync), so the residual window is
+// classic-mode fallback (persistent boot failed/pending) overlapping with a
